1
00:00:01,611 --> 00:00:05,165
The Great Showdown! Giant VS Giant!

2
00:00:07,333 --> 00:00:09,612
Turn right at the next intersection, please.

3
00:00:09,612 --> 00:00:10,852
Okaaay.

4
00:00:10,852 --> 00:00:13,820
Crest! Don't you think you can tell us now?

5
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:16,120
Yeah! Where are we going?

6
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:19,664
I told you, this is a mystery tour to a surprise location.

7
00:00:19,664 --> 00:00:21,811
So we'll find out when we get there.

8
00:00:21,811 --> 00:00:26,103
Oh well... Crest is all about the secrets, I see.

9
00:00:26,103 --> 00:00:29,245
No. He is just serious, intelligent, and can keep his mouth shut.

10
00:00:29,245 --> 00:00:32,125
Yeah, yeah! The opposite of someone else we know!

11
00:00:32,125 --> 00:00:33,914
And who might that be?

12
00:00:33,914 --> 00:00:35,621
Don't let that get to you, Jun.

13
00:00:35,621 --> 00:00:37,780
And what do you mean by that, Blue Cop?!

14
00:00:47,398 --> 00:00:48,411
Here we are.

15
00:00:48,521 --> 00:00:50,853
Our destination was Mowtown's landfill?

16
00:00:50,853 --> 00:00:52,633
I've never been here before...

17
00:00:52,633 --> 00:00:55,292
Now, can you tell us why you've brought us here?

18
00:00:55,292 --> 00:00:57,277
Yes. Because of this.

19
00:00:58,573 --> 00:00:59,999
That thing on the map?

20
00:00:59,999 --> 00:01:00,920
Correct.

21
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:02,365
What is that blinky thing?

22
00:01:02,365 --> 00:01:06,932
The signal from a GPS transmitter attached to Heavy Iron.

23
00:01:06,932 --> 00:01:08,349
Heavy Iron?!

24
00:01:11,364 --> 00:01:15,137
Do you know what you're doing?! Heavy Iron isn't one to be messed with!

25
00:01:15,137 --> 00:01:17,870
Mhm. I heard from Wild Guardy.

26
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:19,402
You knew, and you still brought us here?!

27
00:01:19,402 --> 00:01:22,174
So you mean... Heavy Iron is here right now?!

28
00:01:22,174 --> 00:01:24,658
Yes, over there.

29
00:01:25,390 --> 00:01:27,114
Waah!

30
00:01:27,114 --> 00:01:29,599
We're too close!

31
00:01:29,599 --> 00:01:30,539
What if we get caught?!

32
00:01:30,539 --> 00:01:34,420
Don't worry! He hasn't moved an inch since I've started tracking him.

33
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:38,932
Oh... so he can't move because of his injuries from the last battle.

34
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:42,860
So... you mean Heavy Iron is sound asleep because he's recovering?

35
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:47,299
That's correct. Metal Cardbots have a self recovering function powered by nanomachines.

36
00:01:47,299 --> 00:01:50,390
But... it's not enough to just sleep it off like that.

37
00:01:50,390 --> 00:01:53,514
It takes up a lot of energy even to heal a single wound.

38
00:01:53,514 --> 00:01:54,721
Energy?

39
00:01:54,721 --> 00:01:58,926
Metal Cardbots are like humans in that way, too. We need energy even if we're not exerting ourselves.

40
00:01:58,926 --> 00:02:00,686
I wonder, what do you guys eat?

41
00:02:00,686 --> 00:02:05,176
We eat all kinds of fuel! Stuff like gasoline, electricity, and methane gas.

42
00:02:05,176 --> 00:02:08,632
A landfill like this is full to the brim with methane gas.

43
00:02:08,632 --> 00:02:10,247
You guys really eat methane?

44
00:02:10,247 --> 00:02:11,575
Sure.

45
00:02:11,575 --> 00:02:14,396
It's a simple pleasure, but the taste is beyond words.

46
00:02:14,396 --> 00:02:18,500
He can't do much while focusing on recovery, so now may be our best chance to seal him.

47
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:21,475
Okay, Blue Cop. We gotta seal him before he makes a move.

48
00:02:21,475 --> 00:02:22,650
Roger that, Jun.

49
00:02:23,990 --> 00:02:25,502
Metal Breath, pickup!

50
00:02:31,180 --> 00:02:32,417
What was that?!

51
00:02:39,110 --> 00:02:41,168
Is that a pirate ship?!

52
00:02:41,168 --> 00:02:42,143
It couldn't be...

53
00:02:42,143 --> 00:02:43,549
Black Hook!

54
00:02:43,549 --> 00:02:44,670
You know him?

55
00:02:44,670 --> 00:02:45,500
Yes.

56
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:48,496
He was an infamous pirate on planet Machina. Everyone knew his name.

57
00:02:48,496 --> 00:02:52,496
Many Star Guardians had tried to apprehend him, but were defeated instead.

58
00:02:54,670 --> 00:02:58,706
Aah! Stop it! You'll wake up Heavy Iron!

59
00:02:59,829 --> 00:03:02,241
Hahaha!

60
00:03:02,241 --> 00:03:11,203
So you've been hiding away in a trash heap. It suits you well, Heavy Iron.

61
00:03:11,203 --> 00:03:12,203
Ah...

62
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:16,854
Where are you keeping the Star Crown? My stolen treasure!

63
00:03:27,961 --> 00:03:29,658
Hmph.

64
00:03:29,658 --> 00:03:31,859
It's been a while, Black Hook.

65
00:03:31,859 --> 00:03:34,944
The Star Crown is safe with me.

66
00:03:34,944 --> 00:03:36,389
Glad to hear it!

67
00:03:36,389 --> 00:03:39,413
There's nothing a pirate likes more than to loot and plunder!

68
00:03:39,413 --> 00:03:42,199
You're just a common thief!

69
00:03:48,871 --> 00:03:51,747
Dealing with one was bad enough, but now there are two of them?!

70
00:03:51,747 --> 00:03:53,786
Jun, what do we do?

71
00:03:53,786 --> 00:03:56,259
Don't worry. This might be a good thing.

72
00:03:56,259 --> 00:03:57,460
Jun's right.

73
00:03:57,460 --> 00:04:00,757
Let them fight it out and seal the one who loses. All we have to do is wait.

74
00:04:00,757 --> 00:04:02,461
Like fishing in troubled waters.

75
00:04:20,672 --> 00:04:21,954
Everyone, run!

76
00:04:29,850 --> 00:04:30,737
Jun!

77
00:04:34,105 --> 00:04:35,795
And who might you be?!

78
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:39,668
I know you. You're the little runt that was controlling Blue Cop.

79
00:04:39,668 --> 00:04:41,319
That kid?!

80
00:04:42,790 --> 00:04:46,389
You mean this Earthling child is the master of a Star Guardian?!

81
00:04:46,389 --> 00:04:48,201
Don't be ridiculous.

82
00:04:48,951 --> 00:04:50,862
I-Is that...

83
00:04:50,862 --> 00:04:54,533
The Metal Breath? Legendary treasure of Deus Machina?!

84
00:04:54,533 --> 00:04:56,218
Hand it over!!

85
00:04:57,117 --> 00:04:59,620
No way! Don't even think about it!

86
00:04:59,620 --> 00:05:01,189
Blue Cop, setup!

87
00:05:02,737 --> 00:05:03,713
Yaah!

88
00:05:07,807 --> 00:05:09,240
Jun. Are you alright?

89
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:10,502
Thank you!

90
00:05:10,502 --> 00:05:13,262
There you are, Blue Cop.

91
00:05:13,262 --> 00:05:16,139
So you're the surviving Star Guardian...

92
00:05:16,139 --> 00:05:19,163
Yes. Even if my home planet no longer exists,

93
00:05:19,163 --> 00:05:22,574
the will of Deus Machina is engraved in my memory circuit.

94
00:05:22,574 --> 00:05:24,278
What a joke!

95
00:05:24,278 --> 00:05:27,843
Black Hook. Let's settle our score some other time.

96
00:05:27,843 --> 00:05:30,711
You're calling a truce, huh?

97
00:05:30,711 --> 00:05:32,281
Guys, get out of here!

98
00:05:32,281 --> 00:05:33,790
Come on, let's go!

99
00:05:34,644 --> 00:05:37,581
I'll take you up on that offer, however...

100
00:05:37,581 --> 00:05:41,252
The legendary treasure is all mine!!

101
00:05:47,369 --> 00:05:49,831
He can't fight them both!

102
00:05:49,831 --> 00:05:51,454
Jun! I'm okay!

103
00:05:51,454 --> 00:05:53,930
Blue Cop, cause a distraction! Hurry!

104
00:05:53,930 --> 00:05:54,939
Got it!

105
00:05:57,466 --> 00:05:59,334
You slippery little pest.

106
00:06:06,603 --> 00:06:07,603
Jun!

107
00:06:07,896 --> 00:06:09,605
I'll be alright. You guys get outta here!

108
00:06:09,605 --> 00:06:10,846
Don't overdo it!

109
00:06:13,298 --> 00:06:15,855
I'll admit you got some guts, small fry!

110
00:06:15,855 --> 00:06:18,370
Now, hand over the Metal Breath!

111
00:06:18,370 --> 00:06:19,937
And what if I don't?!

112
00:06:20,677 --> 00:06:22,290
Shadow X, setup!

113
00:06:22,865 --> 00:06:25,456
Yeah! Haha!

114
00:06:25,610 --> 00:06:28,468
Shadow X, launch your Spinning Cutter from the air!

115
00:06:29,502 --> 00:06:30,968
Spinning Cutter!

116
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:36,750
That hurt!

117
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:36,773
Huh?

118
00:06:38,742 --> 00:06:40,187
Heli-Tornado!

119
00:06:40,382 --> 00:06:42,509
Heli-Tornado!

120
00:06:47,987 --> 00:06:49,667
Huh? Where did that small fry go?!

121
00:06:50,413 --> 00:06:52,557
Ahoy matey! Where ya lookin'?!

122
00:06:56,862 --> 00:06:59,295
You annoying little fruit fly!

123
00:06:59,507 --> 00:07:01,543
Just keep it up a little longer, Shadow X!

124
00:07:01,543 --> 00:07:03,451
Leave it to me! Over here, ye salty dog!

125
00:07:03,451 --> 00:07:05,793
Blue Cop, we'll be there shortly.

126
00:07:05,793 --> 00:07:08,560
We have to seal Heavy Iron as soon as possible!

127
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:09,903
Roger that!

128
00:07:09,903 --> 00:07:12,446
Enough with this game of tag!

129
00:07:23,836 --> 00:07:24,853
Blue Cop!

130
00:07:25,797 --> 00:07:28,233
Not so tough now, are you?

131
00:07:28,233 --> 00:07:30,730
Wild Guardy, we need to hurry!

132
00:07:30,730 --> 00:07:31,197
Got it!

133
00:07:35,725 --> 00:07:38,490
Now it's time to end you once and for all!

134
00:07:43,997 --> 00:07:45,451
Metal Breath, pickup!

135
00:07:47,211 --> 00:07:48,800
Wild Guardy, setup!

136
00:07:58,855 --> 00:07:59,622
I'll be your opponent!

137
00:08:01,389 --> 00:08:03,088
You again?

138
00:08:06,399 --> 00:08:08,915
I'll pay you back for this wound a hundredfold!

139
00:08:08,915 --> 00:08:10,514
Not interested!

140
00:08:14,134 --> 00:08:16,954
Start playing fair and show yourself!

141
00:08:17,906 --> 00:08:20,319
A pirate wants to play fair? Don't make me laugh!

142
00:08:23,682 --> 00:08:25,353
There you are!

143
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:30,523
Where did you run off to, Earthling child?!

144
00:08:33,134 --> 00:08:35,263
Where is the pirate going now?

145
00:08:35,263 --> 00:08:37,139
Uncle Edo! We need to go after him!

146
00:08:37,139 --> 00:08:39,907
Oh- uh, alright! Everyone, hold on tight!

147
00:08:52,354 --> 00:08:54,418
Keep it up! Wild Slash!

148
00:08:54,470 --> 00:08:55,524
Wild...

149
00:08:55,524 --> 00:08:56,509
Slash!

150
00:09:04,591 --> 00:09:07,677
I'd like to keep playing, but let's end this now.

151
00:09:07,677 --> 00:09:10,230
I still need to get some rest.

152
00:09:10,230 --> 00:09:11,610
Hurry up and get out of there!

153
00:09:14,831 --> 00:09:16,239
He's not gonna try that...

154
00:09:19,854 --> 00:09:21,937
Hey, Heavy Iron!

155
00:09:23,628 --> 00:09:26,308
If you fire that, you'll also blow the Metal Breath to smithereens!

156
00:09:26,308 --> 00:09:28,221
That's none of my concern.

157
00:09:28,221 --> 00:09:29,739
You piece of...

158
00:09:29,739 --> 00:09:31,403
That wasn't part of the deal!

159
00:09:31,403 --> 00:09:34,320
I never made a deal with you!

160
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:37,388
Captain's Cannon!

161
00:09:39,639 --> 00:09:41,605
Iron Cannon!

162
00:09:47,951 --> 00:09:49,317
Over there!

163
00:09:51,586 --> 00:09:52,947
Could they be...

164
00:09:52,947 --> 00:09:53,821
Jun...

165
00:09:57,307 --> 00:09:58,230
Wild Guardy!

166
00:09:58,356 --> 00:09:59,615
Jun is okay.

167
00:09:59,615 --> 00:10:03,197
I thought I was done for this time...

168
00:10:03,197 --> 00:10:05,364
That brought back some bad memories...

169
00:10:05,364 --> 00:10:06,543
What a relief.

170
00:10:06,543 --> 00:10:08,480
Do you think either one of them is down?

171
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:09,793
I don't think so.

172
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:12,870
Ugh... I can't believe this...

173
00:10:12,870 --> 00:10:16,802
I only came for my Star Crown, but found myself in this mess!

174
00:10:16,802 --> 00:10:19,875
Earthling child! That will be all for today.

175
00:10:19,875 --> 00:10:22,331
I'll be back for your Metal Breath soon,

176
00:10:22,331 --> 00:10:24,965
so take good care of it until I return!

177
00:10:24,965 --> 00:10:26,557
Hahaha!

178
00:10:26,557 --> 00:10:28,690
Jun, what about Heavy Iron?

179
00:10:28,690 --> 00:10:30,596
I don't think that was enough to finish him off.

180
00:10:30,596 --> 00:10:34,662
There's no use in sticking around. Let's get out of here!

181
00:10:44,418 --> 00:10:45,812
Aah!

182
00:10:45,812 --> 00:10:47,763
Hey, be gentle with that!

183
00:10:47,763 --> 00:10:49,149
Ugh. Stop complaining.

184
00:10:49,149 --> 00:10:50,911
Wild Guardy is fine.

185
00:10:50,911 --> 00:10:53,378
Just a little tear in the fuel hose. I replaced it.

186
00:10:53,378 --> 00:10:54,850
That's good to hear.

187
00:10:54,850 --> 00:10:56,850
Those two were really scary.

188
00:10:56,850 --> 00:11:01,875
Heavy Iron and Black Hook. Two really strong Cardbots showed up at once!

189
00:11:01,875 --> 00:11:05,177
If we're going to want to seal them, we'll have to get stronger too.

190
00:11:05,177 --> 00:11:06,937
Yes, Jun!

191
00:11:07,548 --> 00:11:10,629
I'll leave it to you guys from now on.

192
00:11:10,629 --> 00:11:12,615
What do you mean, Crest?

193
00:11:12,615 --> 00:11:15,408
The thing is, I realize how foolish I've been.

194
00:11:15,408 --> 00:11:18,360
In the future, I'll try to help you in different ways.

195
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:19,278
Crest!

196
00:11:19,490 --> 00:11:22,793
Please take care of Wild Guardy, Jun.

197
00:11:24,738 --> 00:11:26,385
Of course!

